<title>TURKEY: TURK UZEL MAKINA H1 NET PROFIT RISES.</title>
<headline>TURK UZEL MAKINA H1 NET PROFIT RISES.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-June 1997 final</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>				  H1 1997	 H1 1996</p>
<p>				  -------	 -------</p>
<p>    Per share profit     1,732.69  vs  42,366.17</p>
<p>    Net Profit	     3,985.19  vs   1,694.65</p>
<p>    Net sales	     21,456.17  vs   9,649.36</p>
<p>    Operating profit     5,409.50  vs   2,367.18</p>
<p>    Exceptional income   1,773.59  vs     727.56</p>
<p>    Interest paid	  1,309.74  vs	 4.22</p>
<p>    Total debts	    7,540.01  vs   3,545.21</p>
<p>    Equity		   7,263.88  vs   2,521.97</p>
<p>    Capital		  2,300.00  vs	40.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Leading Turkish tractor producer Uzel Makina Sanayii A.S. floated 345 billion lira of its capital on July 30-31. 85 percent of the offer was sold abroad and the floated shares were listed on the Istanbul stock market on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Part of the shares sold abroad were also listed on the London Stock Exchange this week in the form of ADSs.</p>
<p>Uzel Makina said this week it would offer an optional 51.75 billion lira worth of shares to investors abroad within 30 days.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 78 percent consumer price inflation in June.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212 275 08 75</p>
